  {
   "file": "合作者组会20260119.pptx",
   "slide": 8,
   "text": "Some suppositions | 7k-LCA, CDCA and DCA, especially 7k-LCA, can bind to VFA0359 mutants much more easily than other bile acid molecules;\nMutations on the edge of pocket may change the pocket tolerance for different molecules by slightly changing the shape of docking pocket and mutations on the core pocket may prefer to disrupt the docking process because these residues may directly interact with the small molecules;\nSome specific mutations on the core pocket may change the binding specificity but we don’t know whether these mutations can be predicted accurately."
  },
